{"page":"PAF1","gene":"PAF1","accession":"Q8N7H5","protein":"RNA polymerase II-associated factor 1 homolog","length":531,"events":["Alternative splicing"],"canonical":{"accession":"Q8N7H5-1","name":"1","synonyms":[],"notes":[],"transcripts":{"ensembl":["ENST00000221265.8"],"refseq":["NM_019088.4"],"refseqProteins":["NP_061961.2"],"maneSelect":true,"decay":[],"onlyDecay":false},"model":{"entry":"AF-Q8N7H5-F1","cif":"https://alphafold.ebi.ac.uk/files/AF-Q8N7H5-F1-model_v6.cif","meanPlddt":66.9,"plddt":[[0,2],[50,2],[0,1],[50,1],[0,16],[50,2],[0,1],[50,3],[70,28],[50,2],[70,1],[50,1],[70,13],[50,1],[70,1],[50,1],[70,13],[90,1],[70,10],[90,2],[70,1],[90,1],[70,6],[50,27],[0,2],[50,2],[0,8],[50,5],[0,2],[50,12],[70,4],[90,1],[70,2],[90,15],[70,1],[90,17],[70,12],[90,3],[70,20],[90,3],[70,13],[90,4],[70,24],[90,3],[70,22],[90,1],[70,1],[90,1],[70,5],[90,3],[70,7],[90,3],[70,3],[50,2],[0,1],[50,2],[0,1],[50,3],[70,4],[90,1],[70,22],[50,2],[0,6],[50,12],[0,47],[50,16],[0,73],[50,3]]}},"features":[{"type":"Modified residue","start":117,"end":117,"description":"Phosphoserine"},{"type":"Cross-link","start":133,"end":133,"description":"Glycyl lysine isopeptide (Lys-Gly) (interchain with G-Cter in SUMO2)"},{"type":"Region","start":150,"end":300,"description":"Interaction with PINT87aa"},{"type":"Cross-link","start":154,"end":154,"description":"Glycyl lysine isopeptide (Lys-Gly) (interchain with G-Cter in SUMO2)"},{"type":"Coiled coil","start":352,"end":400,"description":""},{"type":"Modified residue","start":456,"end":456,"description":"Phosphoserine"}],"interfaces":{},"subunit":[{"topic":"Subunit","text":"Component of the PAF1 complex, which consists of CDC73, PAF1, LEO1, CTR9, RTF1 and SKIC8 (PubMed:19952111, PubMed:20178742). The PAF1 complex interacts with PHF5A (By similarity). Interacts with POLR2A, TCEA1, SKIC3, KMT2A/MLL1, SUPT5H, RNF20 and RNF40 (PubMed:15923622, PubMed:16024656, PubMed:16491129, PubMed:19410543, PubMed:19952111, PubMed:20178742, PubMed:20541477). Interacts with UBE2E1 (PubMed:16307923). Interacts with PINT87aa which is encoded by the circular form of the long non-coding RNA LINC-PINT; the interaction enhances the binding of the PAF1 complex to target gene promoters and may anchor the complex on target gene promoters, sequentially pausing RNA polymerase II-induced mRNA elongation (PubMed:30367041)"},{"topic":"Subunit","text":"(Microbial infection) Interacts with influenza A strain H3N2 NS1 protein; the interaction interferes with host cell gene transcription, specifically with that of antiviral genes"},{"topic":"Subunit","text":"(Microbial infection) The PAF1 complex interacts with Zika virus French Polynesia 10087PF/2013 non-structural protein 5/NS5 (PubMed:30550790). The interaction with viral NS5 proteins may reduce the antiviral immune response by inhibiting the recruitment of the PAF1 complex to interferon-stimulated genes, thus preventing their transcription (PubMed:30550790)"},{"topic":"Subunit","text":"(Microbial infection) The PAF1 complex interacts with Dengue virus DENV2 16681 non-structural protein 5/NS5 (PubMed:30550790). The PAF1 complex interacts with Dengue virus DENV4 Dominica/814669/1981 non-structural protein 5/NS5 (PubMed:30550790). The interaction with viral NS5 proteins may reduce the antiviral immune response by inhibiting the recruitment of the PAF1 complex to interferon-stimulated genes, thus preventing their transcription (PubMed:30550790)"}],"isoforms":[{"accession":"Q8N7H5-2","name":"2","synonyms":[],"notes":[],"length":485,"transcripts":{"ensembl":[],"refseq":[],"refseqProteins":[],"maneSelect":false,"decay":[],"onlyDecay":false},"segments":[[1,1,16],[17,27,163],[180,213,182],[463,509,23]],"edits":[{"start":17,"end":26,"original":"PNSHRTLPER","replacement":"","added":0},{"start":190,"end":212,"original":"ISQHYSKPRVTPVEVMPVFPDFK","replacement":"","added":0},{"start":395,"end":508,"original":"DEEQEKGSSSEKEGSEDEHSGSESEREEGDRDEASDKSGS","replacement":"VMLILRTMPTLMMRTEDRPKVAVTMIQTAAAMGVASGAG